  "title": "Why does this window turn into a mirror?",
  "series": "Field Study / Optics",
  "bgMusic": "synthwave_tense",
  "narration": "Why does this window turn into a mirror at night? Watch the glass. Sunlight shoots straight through it and hits your eyes. From inside, the room light hits your face. Some of that light bounces off the very same glass and comes right back to you. Both pictures are there at once! By day the street is so bright it buries your reflection. After sunset the street goes dark, but your face is still lit. Now your reflection wins. Cup your hands against the glass. Block that room light and the street pops back. Peel your hands away and there's your face again. And that is exactly…",
